meta {
  name: List Carriers
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/carriers
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("returns a carriers array", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body).to.have.property("carriers");
    expect(body.carriers).to.be.an("array");
    expect(body.carriers.length).to.be.above(0);
  });

  test("every carrier carries the four option fields", function () {
    for (const carrier of res.getBody().carriers) {
      expect(carrier).to.have.property("id");
      expect(carrier).to.have.property("name");
      expect(carrier).to.have.property("policyNumberPattern");
      expect(carrier).to.have.property("policyNumberHint");
    }
  });

  test("Allstate is present and sorts first", function () {
    const carriers = res.getBody().carriers;
    expect(carriers[0].name).to.equal("Allstate");
  });

  test("Allstate carries the digits-only rule", function () {
    const allstate = res.getBody().carriers.find((c) => c.name === "Allstate");
    expect(allstate.policyNumberPattern).to.equal("\\d+");
    expect(allstate.policyNumberHint).to.be.a("string");
  });

  test("carriers we have no format for carry a null pattern", function () {
    const unconstrained = res
      .getBody()
      .carriers.filter((c) => c.policyNumberPattern === null);
    expect(unconstrained.length).to.be.above(0);
  });

  test("never leaks the internal slug", function () {
    for (const carrier of res.getBody().carriers) {
      expect(carrier).to.not.have.property("slug");
      expect(carrier).to.not.have.property("agencyId");
    }
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /carriers — the carrier vocabulary (PAC-56 #19)

  The list behind the Sold wizard's **carrier select** (#18) and its
  **per-carrier policy-number rules** (#20). Returns platform-global carriers
  unioned with the calling agency's own rows.

  - **Module:** `deal_audits` (must be enabled for the agency)
  - **Permission:** `deal_audits:read`
  - **Data scope:** none — reference data, identical for everyone in the agency

  > **Why `deal_audits` and not a `carriers` module?** The list exists to serve
  > the Sold form, so it carries the Sold form's gate — the same argument
  > `GET /policies/check` makes. A dedicated `ModuleKey.Carriers` would add a row
  > to the permission matrix (one entry per module key) for something that is not
  > a page, and give every agency a second switch that can silently break the
  > wizard.
  >
  > ⚠ Consequence: disabling the `deal_audits` module also disables this list,
  > and therefore the carrier select.

  ## Two kinds of row
  A carrier document carries `agencyId: string | null`.

  | `agencyId` | meaning | who writes it |
  |---|---|---|
  | `null` | platform global, visible to every agency | the core seed (`seedCarriers`) |
  | an id | that agency's own addition | future agency-owner CRUD |

  An agency row **shadows** a global with the same slug, so an agency can
  override a global's display name or pattern rather than having to invent a
  different name to avoid the clash. Only globals exist today.

  Neither `slug` nor `agencyId` is returned — both are internal.

  ## Curation is deliberately not here
  Seeding only. Super-admin CRUD belongs at `platform/carriers` under
  `platform:*`; agency-owner CRUD under `agency:*`. The schema already carries
  `agencyId`, `active` and `displayOrder` so both drop in as controllers with no
  schema change.

  ## Where the list came from
  ⚠ **Not from migrated data.** Legacy's Policies `Carrier` (`s33be9b77d`) is a
  single-select with exactly one choice, `B4tEH` = Allstate, and the
  prior-insurance carrier fields were plain strings. Allstate is the only name
  with legacy authority; the other sixteen are our proposal.

  ## `policyNumberPattern`
  A regex **source**, stored **unanchored**, tested against the *normalized*
  policy-number key (uppercase, non-alphanumerics stripped) so `123-456`
  satisfies a digits-only rule. The consumer anchors it —
  `carrierPolicyNumberMatches` wraps it as `^(?:pattern)$` — so a pattern can
  never accidentally match a substring.

  `null` means the carrier imposes no format. **Only Allstate carries one.** A
  wrong rule fails closed — it blocks a real sale, and with no admin UI the only
  fix is a deploy — so a pattern is seeded only where we are certain. We know
  Allstate is digits-only; we do not know its length, hence `\d+` rather than a
  bounded form.

  Enforced server-side in `POST /sold-deals` and on `PATCH /policies/:id` when
  the number changes. The wizard validates live off the same data; that is an
  assist, not the gate.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "carriers": [
      {
        "id": "665f...ac1",
        "name": "Allstate",
        "policyNumberPattern": "\\d+",
        "policyNumberHint": "Allstate policy numbers are digits only."
      },
      {
        "id": "665f...ac2",
        "name": "State Farm",
        "policyNumberPattern": null,
        "policyNumberHint": null
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  Sorted by `displayOrder` then `name`, so Allstate — the agency's own carrier —
  is first. Inactive carriers (`active: false`) are never returned.

  ## The "Other" escape
  The wizard renders an **Other** choice that reveals a free-text box, so an
  unseeded carrier never blocks a sale. That is a client-side sentinel
  (`CARRIER_OTHER`) resolved to the typed name before submission; the API rejects
  the sentinel outright, so it can never be stored as a carrier name. A carrier
  absent from this list carries no pattern and is therefore unvalidated.

  ## Errors
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired access token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — `deal_audits` module disabled, or missing `deal_audits:read`.

  ## Run order
  No dependencies — only `Auth/Login` for the token. Bruno walks folders
  alphabetically, so this runs early and needs nothing seeded beyond
  `npm run api:seed:dev`.
}
